# =============================================================================
# TicketFlow — Root .gitignore
# Covers all 10 services: config-server, service-discovery, api-gateway,
# auth-service, user-service, venue-service, seat-inventory-service,
# booking-orchestration-service, payment-service, notification-service
#
# Stack: Spring Boot 3.3.x / Java 21 / Maven / PostgreSQL / Redis /
#         Kafka / MongoDB / Docker / Kubernetes / GitHub Actions
# =============================================================================


# =============================================================================
# SECRETS & CREDENTIALS — NEVER COMMIT THESE
# A single leaked private key or DB password in Git history is an incident.
# These patterns apply across all service directories.
# =============================================================================

# RSA key pairs — auth-service uses RSA-256 to sign JWTs.
# Private key MUST never be in VCS. Public key is safe but excluded for hygiene.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
*.pfx
*.crt
*.cer
*.der

# Environment variable files — used for local docker-compose overrides.
# Real values live in K8s Secrets / AWS Secrets Manager / Vault in prod.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Spring Boot environment-specific configs that contain real secrets.
# The config-server pulls these from a SEPARATE private Git repo at runtime.
# Local overrides with real DB passwords, Redis passwords, Kafka credentials
# must never land in this repo.
#
# Pattern: application-{env}.yml files at service level are fine IF they
# contain only non-secret overrides (log levels, feature flags, timeouts).
# The moment a file contains a password, token, or key — it must go in
# the config-server's private backing repo, not here.
#
# We exclude the most dangerous patterns:
**/src/main/resources/application-prod.yml
**/src/main/resources/application-staging.yml
**/src/main/resources/bootstrap-prod.yml
**/src/main/resources/bootstrap-staging.yml

# K8s Secret manifests — these should be generated by Helm/Kustomize at
# deploy time from a secret store, never stored as plaintext YAML.
k8s/secrets/
**/secret.yaml
**/secrets.yaml
**/*-secret.yaml
**/*-secrets.yaml

# Cloud provider credentials
.aws/
.gcp/
*.json.credentials
service-account*.json
gcp-credentials*.json

# Vault / Secrets Manager token files
.vault-token
vault-token


# =============================================================================
# MAVEN BUILD ARTIFACTS
# Each of the 10 services has its own Maven build lifecycle.
# =============================================================================

# Compiled output — generated by mvn compile / mvn package
target/

# Per-module Maven wrapper cache
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties

# Maven local repository cache (never commit — multi-GB)
.m2/

# Surefire test reports (generated by mvn test)
# HTML reports go here: target/surefire-reports/
# We exclude at the root level; each service's target/ already covers it.

# Failsafe integration test reports (generated by mvn verify)
# target/failsafe-reports/ — covered by target/ exclusion above


# =============================================================================
# SPRING BOOT RUNTIME ARTIFACTS
# =============================================================================

# Executable JARs produced by spring-boot-maven-plugin repackage goal.
# These are built by CI/CD and pushed to ECR — never committed to VCS.
*.jar
*.war
*.ear

# Spring Boot DevTools restart trigger file
.spring-boot-devtools.properties
spring-devtools.properties

# Spring Boot application PID file (created when app starts with spring.pid.file)
*.pid
application.pid

# Spring Shell history
.spring-shell.log


# =============================================================================
# ENVIRONMENT-SPECIFIC CONFIGURATION STRATEGY
#
# TicketFlow uses Spring Cloud Config Server backed by a SEPARATE private
# Git repository (not this one). Here is the full config file hierarchy:
#
# LOCAL DEV (docker-compose):
#   Each service: src/main/resources/application.yml       ← committed (no secrets)
#                 src/main/resources/application-local.yml ← committed (local ports, no secrets)
#   docker-compose.yml                                      ← committed
#   docker-compose.override.yml                            ← NOT committed (local port overrides)
#
# STAGING / PROD (Kubernetes + Config Server):
#   Config server pulls from private Git repo at startup.
#   K8s ConfigMaps: non-secret env-specific values         ← committed under k8s/
#   K8s Secrets: generated at deploy time from Vault       ← NEVER committed
#
# Files excluded below reinforce this strategy.
# =============================================================================

# Docker Compose local override files — developer-specific port/volume overrides
docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.override.yaml

# Local config overrides that may contain developer-specific values
**/application-local-override.yml


# =============================================================================
# LOGS
# Structured JSON logs (our format per system design Section 11) are shipped
# to ELK via Filebeat. Log files must never accumulate in the repo.
# =============================================================================

logs/
*.log
*.log.*
*.log.gz
*.log.zip

# Per-service log directories
**/logs/
**/*.log

# Logback lock files
*.lck


# =============================================================================
# INTELLIJ IDEA
# Standard for Spring Boot / Java shops. Exclude workspace-specific files
# but commit .idea/modules.xml and *.iml if the team agrees — here we
# exclude everything for maximum portability.
# =============================================================================

.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
out/
.idea_modules/

# IntelliJ HTTP Client environment files (may contain local API keys/tokens)
# The public .http files are fine to commit; the environment file is not.
http-client.private.env.json
http-client.env.json


# =============================================================================
# ECLIPSE / STS (Spring Tool Suite)
# =============================================================================

.classpath
.project
.settings/
.factorypath
bin/
!**/src/main/**/bin/
!**/src/test/**/bin/


# =============================================================================
# VS CODE
# =============================================================================

.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json


# =============================================================================
# DOCKER BUILD ARTIFACTS
# Dockerfiles are committed (they're infrastructure-as-code).
# Generated artifacts from Docker builds are not.
# =============================================================================

# Docker layer cache
.docker/

# Buildkit cache mount directories
.buildcache/

# docker-compose generated volumes config (not the compose file itself)
docker-compose.volumes.yml


# =============================================================================
# KUBERNETES — GENERATED ARTIFACTS
# Raw K8s manifests under k8s/ ARE committed (deployment.yaml, service.yaml,
# hpa.yaml, configmap.yaml per service per system design Section 12).
# Generated/rendered artifacts from Helm or Kustomize are not.
# =============================================================================

# Helm chart lock file (contains resolved dependencies — can be regenerated)
**/charts/*.lock

# Helm rendered output (generated by helm template, not source of truth)
helm-output/
rendered/

# Kustomize build output
kustomize-output/

# Skaffold build artifacts
.skaffold/


# =============================================================================
# TESTCONTAINERS & INTEGRATION TEST ARTIFACTS
# Testcontainers spins up real PostgreSQL, Redis, Kafka per Section 12.
# It generates temporary files and cached images that must not be committed.
# =============================================================================

# Testcontainers local properties (Ryuk reuse config, custom Docker host)
.testcontainers.properties
testcontainers.properties

# Ryuk container state
.ryuk/


# =============================================================================
# OBSERVABILITY — LOCAL ARTIFACTS
# In local dev, we run Jaeger, Prometheus, Grafana via docker-compose.
# Their data directories and exported dashboards (auto-generated) are excluded.
# Manually crafted Grafana dashboard JSON files SHOULD be committed under
# k8s/monitoring/ or observability/ — those are not excluded here.
# =============================================================================

# Prometheus data directory (when running locally)
prometheus-data/
grafana-data/
jaeger-data/

# OpenTelemetry collector local state
otel-collector-data/


# =============================================================================
# OS & SYSTEM FILES
# =============================================================================

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Windows
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# Linux
*~
.nfs*


# =============================================================================
# SONARQUBE & CODE QUALITY
# =============================================================================

# SonarQube analysis cache (generated by sonar:sonar goal)
.sonar/
.scannerwork/

# JaCoCo coverage reports (generated by mvn verify)
# target/site/jacoco/ — covered by target/ exclusion
# But explicit exclusion in case reports are generated outside target/
jacoco.exec
jacoco-it.exec


# =============================================================================
# GITHUB ACTIONS — LOCAL SIMULATION ARTIFACTS
# GitHub Actions workflow files under .github/workflows/ ARE committed.
# Local act (https://github.com/nektos/act) simulation artifacts are not.
# =============================================================================

.act/


# =============================================================================
# MISCELLANEOUS
# =============================================================================

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.swp
*.swo

# Patch files
*.patch
*.diff

# Archive files (should never be in source control)
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.tar
*.rar
*.7z

# NPM (in case any tooling/frontend scaffolding is added later)
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Python virtualenv (in case any ops/migration scripts are added)
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc